# SPEC: 65_symbol_clearance
# Requires: driver
# static-check: off
# NEEDS: write
# CLEARANCE: 7
# NEGATIVE (spec/65 F65-32): the policy is readable, never writable.  A builtin that
# SETS `create_level` would be self-certification (F65-6) — the script would grant itself a
# right.  So there is no setter, and so that this does not become a silent "unknown function",
# the namespace `clearance` is closed from the ground up (F65-35) and only the three readers are open:
# reaching for a setter names the reason instead of looking like a typo.
# EXPECT-ERROR: clearance-builtin
- def:
    name: main
    return: i32
    body:
      - call: [clearance.set_level, 1]
      - return: [0]
